pokebw2-workareas.patch (tools/pokebw2_fetch.sh, the maintainers' notes): the areas that works with pointers fill, twice their DS
size on a PC target (Black's include/work_area.h, WORK_AREA_SIZE, which port/meson.build -includes for Black 2): the
heap system's root and child heaps (heapsys.c) and heap 9's OS block (gfl_use.c), the field's and the trade screen's
static heap memory, the sound heap (its block headers are 0x60 bytes on a 64-bit host, 0x20 on the DS) and the particle
systems' 0x4800-byte works (the SPL manager's emitters and particles hold pointers: Black's NEW GAME crash) and the wireless helper's WM
buffer (wih.c: WM_SYSTEM_BUF_SIZE is 0x1e00 on a PC target, and WM_Init wants the buffer 32-byte aligned, which the
work's fields before it no longer give: Black 2's C-Gear YES to the wireless failed WM_Init and crashed in the beacon
search). Black's
commits 91c2113ab, 769422881, 46946af9e, 5713cae22 for Black's files.

